{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-09-05T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Rising above the salt marshes along Germany's North Sea coast, the Westerheversand Lighthouse is instantly recognisable thanks to its distinctive red-and-white stripes. Built between 1906 and 1908, the lighthouse has stood as an icon on the Eiderstedt Peninsula for more than a century, guiding ships through the waters of the North Sea. Today, it remains one of northern Germany's best-known coastal landmarks. Visitors who climb its 157 steps are rewarded with sweeping views of the surrounding scenery.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Westerheversand_ROW0428047340_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Westerheversand_ROW0428047340_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Westerheversand Lighthouse in Westerhever, Schleswig-Holstein, Germany","Copyright":"© bluejayphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260904_Westerheversand\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Westerheversand+Lighthouse&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260904_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260904_Westerheversand"},"Ssd":"20260904","Name":"Westerheversand","Market":"ROW","Hash":"0428047340","FullDateString":"Sept 4, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Blink and you'll miss the turn, but you definitely won't miss the cliffs. Vermilion Cliffs National Monument stretches across northern Arizona and protects a landscape shaped over nearly 200 million years. The area became a national monument in 2000, helping safeguard fragile rock formations, prehistoric sites and habitats for rare wildlife. Coyote Buttes is the star attraction for many visitors. Its famous Wave is carved into Navajo Sandstone, which began as vast sand dunes during the Jurassic Period. Over millions of years, wind erosion, rainfall and temperature changes sculpted the flowing bands and curves seen today.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AZWilderness_ROW6879233352_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AZWilderness_ROW6879233352_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Coyote Buttes, Vermilion Cliffs National Monument, Arizona, United States","Copyright":"© James Hager/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260903_AZWilderness\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Vermilion+Cliffs+National+Monument&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260903_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260903_AZWilderness"},"Ssd":"20260903","Name":"AZWilderness","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6879233352","FullDateString":"Sept 3, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Along England's east shore, the Suffolk Heritage Coast blends windswept heaths, marshes, shingle beaches and expansive North Sea views. One of its best-known towns is Southwold, where water and history are inseparable. Almost encircled by the sea, the River Blyth and surrounding wetlands, the town occupies a slender peninsula shaped by centuries of fishing, trade and life at the edge of the water.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SuffolkHuts_ROW5530395883_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SuffolkHuts_ROW5530395883_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Traditional beach huts, Southwold, Suffolk Heritage Coast, England","Copyright":"© stevendocwra/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260902_SuffolkHuts\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Southwold+Suffolk&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260902_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260902_SuffolkHuts"},"Ssd":"20260902","Name":"SuffolkHuts","Market":"ROW","Hash":"5530395883","FullDateString":"Sept 2, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Fungi often go unnoticed beneath forest floors, lawns and fallen leaves, yet their underground threads help recycle nutrients and support healthy ecosystems. The mushrooms we see are only the fruiting bodies of much larger organisms. They appear briefly, release spores, then disappear from sight. Unlike plants, fungi belong to a kingdom of their own. Some species even glow, while others form partnerships with trees.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HorseHairShroom_ROW4884226471_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HorseHairShroom_ROW4884226471_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Horsehair parachute fungus, Belarus","Copyright":"© Máté/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260901_HorseHairShroom\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Fungus&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260901_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260901_HorseHairShroom"},"Ssd":"20260901","Name":"HorseHairShroom","Market":"ROW","Hash":"4884226471","FullDateString":"Sept 1, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"When the first rays of sunlight gild the horizon, Sellin Pier reveals its most striking side. Located on the eastern coast of the island of Rügen in Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, this structure is one of the best-known landmarks on Germany's Baltic coast. Its history dates back to 1906, when the first pier was opened. Over the decades, the structure suffered repeated damage from storms and other factors and was eventually demolished.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SellinSunrise_ROW9214234977_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SellinSunrise_ROW9214234977_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Sellin Pier, Rügen, Germany","Copyright":"© bluejayphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260831_SellinSunrise\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sellin+Pier&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260831_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260831_SellinSunrise"},"Ssd":"20260831","Name":"SellinSunrise","Market":"ROW","Hash":"9214234977","FullDateString":"Aug 31, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Imagine coming face to face with a fish the size of a bus. The whale shark is the world's largest fish, yet it is a remarkably gentle giant. Despite its name, it is not a whale but a shark, with the biggest confirmed individuals measuring around 18 metres long and weighing more than 20 tonnes. Found in warm tropical and subtropical seas, whale sharks move slowly through the water with their mouths open, filtering plankton, fish eggs and other tiny prey. Their distinctive white spots and stripes form patterns unique to each individual, allowing researchers to identify and track them over time.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_ROW3439446140_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_ROW3439446140_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Whale shark and golden trevally, Cenderawasih Bay, West Papua, Indonesia","Copyright":"© Pete Oxford/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260830_YellowShark\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Whale+shark&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260830_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260830_YellowShark"},"Ssd":"20260830","Name":"YellowShark","Market":"ROW","Hash":"3439446140","FullDateString":"Aug 30, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"From the cliffs of Lloret de Mar in Girona, Catalonia, the Camí de Ronda winds along the Costa Brava, a coastline true to its name: wild, rugged and full of surprises. This historic route passes hidden coves, rocky outcrops battered by the Mediterranean and pine forests that reach almost to the sea. It was originally established so that customs officers could patrol the coastline and help prevent smuggling. Today, it is considered one of the most spectacular coastal walks in Spain.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LloretdeMar_ROW9048268267_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LloretdeMar_ROW9048268267_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Camí de Ronda, Lloret de Mar, Catalonia, Spain","Copyright":"© MEDITERRANEAN/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260829_LloretdeMar\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Cami+de+Ronda&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260829_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260829_LloretdeMar"},"Ssd":"20260829","Name":"LloretdeMar","Market":"ROW","Hash":"9048268267","FullDateString":"Aug 29, jjjj"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In September, the French Riviera is bathed in a softer light, and the Mediterranean landscape takes on fresher tones after the peak of summer. The hills are scented with Aleppo pine, rosemary and wild thyme. In the hinterland, centuries-old olive trees and hilltop villages tell a story shaped by Greek, Roman and Provençal influences.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FrenchRivieraVillage_ROW4972919500_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FrenchRivieraVillage_ROW4972919500_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Villefranche-sur-Mer, French Riviera, France","Copyright":"© StockByM/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260911_FrenchRivieraVillage\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Villefranche-sur-Mer&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260911_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260911_FrenchRivieraVillage"},"Ssd":"20260911","Name":"FrenchRivieraVillage","Market":"ROW","Hash":"4972919500","FullDateString":"Sept 11, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Ever wondered why Andalusia is one of Spain's best-known regions? Flamenco, tapas, Moorish architecture and extensive olive groves all play a part. Beyond its famous cities, you'll find historic places like Olvera. Surrounded by more than 2 million olive trees, this village developed as a strategic frontier settlement shaped by centuries of change. The Castle of Olvera still watches over the town, while the Church of Our Lady of the Incarnation dominates the skyline below. Visit La Cilla Cultural Centre to discover Olvera's medieval history and traditions.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Olvera_ROW4122833130_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Olvera_ROW4122833130_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Aerial view of Olvera, Andalusia, Spain","Copyright":"© Marco Bottigelli/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260910_Olvera\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Olvera+Andalusia+Spain&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260910_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260910_Olvera"},"Ssd":"20260910","Name":"Olvera","Market":"ROW","Hash":"4122833130","FullDateString":"Sept 10, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As morning breaks over Elliston, a small seabird appears with a wild iris held across its bill. The scene looks almost like a gift, yet biologists say Atlantic puffins are not known to offer flowers to their mates during courtship. The colourful bill, which becomes brightest in the breeding season and fades later in the year, helps make the photograph memorable. Even their feet turn brighter.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PurplePuffin_ROW7550028597_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PurplePuffin_ROW7550028597_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Atlantic puffin holding a wild iris in his beak in Elliston, Newfoundland, Canada","Copyright":"© mlorenzphotography/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260909_PurplePuffin\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Atlantic+puffin&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260909_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260909_PurplePuffin"},"Ssd":"20260909","Name":"PurplePuffin","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7550028597","FullDateString":"Sept 9, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A beech tree stands alone amid golden fields near East Meon in Hampshire, providing a striking focal point in the rolling landscape of England's South Downs National Park. Agriculture has shaped these chalk hills for centuries, and farming remains an important part of the region today. The area's free-draining chalk soils support extensive arable farming, with wheat and barley among the most common crops. Throughout the summer, these crops ripen in the fields before harvest transforms the countryside into a patchwork of gold and stubble.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BeechEngland_ROW3028721183_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BeechEngland_ROW3028721183_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Beech tree in a cereal field, East Meon, South Downs National Park, Hampshire, England","Copyright":"© Guy Edwardes/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260908_BeechEngland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Hampshire+England&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260908_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260908_BeechEngland"},"Ssd":"20260908","Name":"BeechEngland","Market":"ROW","Hash":"3028721183","FullDateString":"Sept 8, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Perched above the Regnitz River, the Old Town Hall is one of Bamberg's most iconic landmarks in Germany. According to local tradition, the building stands on an artificial island because the town's bishop refused to grant the citizens land for their town hall. In response, residents are said to have created their own site in the middle of the river, giving the structure its remarkable setting and enduring appeal.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BambergTownhall_ROW2569522095_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BambergTownhall_ROW2569522095_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Old Town Hall, Bamberg, Germany","Copyright":"© SCStock/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260907_BambergTownhall\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Bamberg+Germany&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260907_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260907_BambergTownhall"},"Ssd":"20260907","Name":"BambergTownhall","Market":"ROW","Hash":"2569522095","FullDateString":"Sept 7, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At first glance, today's image looks more like a drowned woodland than a lake. Bare tree trunks emerge from the water, their reflections stretching across the surface as the Grampians glow in the distance. This is Lake Fyans, an artificial reservoir on the edge of the Grampians (Gariwerd) National Park in Victoria, Australia. Popular with boaters, anglers, sailors and water skiers, it offers a front-row seat to one of the country's most striking landscapes.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LakeFyans_ROW1462162104_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LakeFyans_ROW1462162104_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Lake Fyans, Grampians National Park, Victoria, Australia","Copyright":"© tracielouise/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260906_LakeFyans\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Grampians+National+Park+Victoria&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260906_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260906_LakeFyans"},"Ssd":"20260906","Name":"LakeFyans","Market":"ROW","Hash":"1462162104","FullDateString":"Sept 6, jjjj"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"When it comes to aerial acrobatics, hummingbirds are in a league of their own. Found only in the Americas, these tiny birds can hover in place, fly backwards and beat their wings dozens of times per second. As they visit flowers in search of nectar, they also serve as important pollinators, helping sustain ecosystems from alpine meadows to tropical rainforests. Their shimmering plumage, remarkable agility and high-energy lifestyles make them some of the world's most fascinating birds.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GreenCrowned_ROW0730008155_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GreenCrowned_ROW0730008155_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Green-crowned brilliant hummingbirds feeding on lobster-claw flowers, Costa Rica","Copyright":"© Paul Hobson/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260905_GreenCrowned\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Green-crowned+brilliant&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260905_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260905_GreenCrowned"},"Ssd":"20260905","Name":"GreenCrowned","Market":"ROW","Hash":"0730008155","FullDateString":"Sept 5, jjjj"}],"LocStrings":{"LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD":"Beeld van die dag","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD_LEARN_MORE":"Kom meer te wete","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_DONATE_NOW":"Skenk nou","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_FACT":"Kitsfeit:","LOC_HOMEPAGE_GALLERY_CARD_TITLE":"Onlangse tuisbladbeelde","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_GALLERY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"Tuisbladbeeld vir {0}","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_TITLE":"Op hierdie dag in geskiedenis","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"Op hierdie dag in {0}, {1}","LOC_HOMEPAGE_SHARE_TOOLTIP":"Deel vandag se Bing-tuisblad","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERDOWNLOAD_TOOLTIP":"Laai hierdie beeld af. Hierdie beeld kan slegs as muurpapier gebruik word.","LOC_MUSCARD_DOWNLOAD_LINK":"Laai hierdie beeld af","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERNOTAVAILABLE":"Hierdie beeld kan nie as muurpapier afgelaai word nie.","LOC_HOMEPAGE_INFO_TEXT":"Inligting","LOC_BING_WP_APP_LINK":"https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?linkid=2127455","LOC_BING_WP_APP_LINK_TEXT":"Kry die Bing-muurpapiertoepassing","LOC_BING_APP_TEXT":"Kry Bing-muurpapier op jou toestelle","LOC_BING_APP_LINK_PC":"https://bing.microsoftapp.net/bing/?adjust=nk9xri2_dzfz5n2","LOC_BING_APP_LINK_MOBILE":"https:/